    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115-a1">

                <pb facs="0286" n="190" xml:id="pg190"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 66.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Luder to Mr. De Espana.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >German Consulate General of Shanghai</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 8, 1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister and Doyen</hi>: The Shanghai Chamber of
                    Commerce has requested, under date of 3d instant, the consular body to forward
                    to your excellency the subjoined request, relative to the measures taken by the
                    Chinese authorities with respect to the hulk of the British firm of Messrs.
                    Butterfield &amp; Swire at Chinkiang. This the consular body is unable to
                    refuse.</p>
                <p>Receive, Mr. minister and Doyen, the assurances of our distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>C. LUDER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General for Germany,
                            Doyen of the Consular Corps.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
